<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately empty.

  AGP synthesises this module's real manifest: the `<instrumentation>` node, its `targetPackage`
  (this module's own, because of `android.experimental.self-instrumenting` in build.gradle.kts),
  and the `<uses-sdk>` from `defaultConfig`. Everything Macrobenchmark itself needs — the
  permissions behind `dumpsys`, `am` and profile capture — is declared in the library's own
  manifest and merged in from there, which is the same reason `app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`
  no longer lists a permission of its own.

  The file exists rather than being absent so that the one thing a test module must never acquire
  is visible as an empty space: a permission or a component added here ships in the APK that runs
  beside the app and changes the thing being measured.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" />
